      "math_academy_id": "e-3019",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} [  3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) ] \\,\\textrm{d}t$ given that $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} \\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 16, \\: 2,\\: -2\\right\\rangle$ and $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2}\\mathbf g(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 2,-4,2\\right\\rangle .$",
      "worked_solution": "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\big[ \\, 3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) \\, \\big] \\, \\textrm d t =  \\displaystyle {3\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t + \\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf g(t) \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[3f(t)+g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3⟨16,\\,2,\\,-2⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨48,\\,6,\\,-6⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨50,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
